---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TopBar from '../components/TopBar.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';

const hreflangAlternates = [
  { hreflang: 'en-CA', href: 'https://www.realtorpeterlaw.com/rent-control/' },
  { hreflang: 'zh-CN', href: 'https://www.realtorpeterlaw.com/chinese/rent-control/' },
  { hreflang: 'fr-CA', href: 'https://www.realtorpeterlaw.com/french/rent-control/' },
  { hreflang: 'x-default', href: 'https://www.realtorpeterlaw.com/rent-control/' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Rent Control in Ontario — Tenant Guide | Peter Law"
  description="Plain-English guide to Ontario rent control: what's covered, the annual guideline, and Above-Guideline Increases."
  bodyClass="guide-page"
  hreflangAlternates={hreflangAlternates}
>

  <TopBar />
  <Header active="rental" />

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Tenant resource</div>
      <h1>Rent control in Ontario.</h1>
      <p>What's covered, what's not, and how the annual cap actually works.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="major" style="padding-top:32px;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose-grid">
        <aside class="prose-side">
          <h4>On this page</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#what">What rent control is</a></li>
            <li><a href="#covered">Which units are covered</a></li>
            <li><a href="#guideline">The annual guideline</a></li>
            <li><a href="#agi">Above-Guideline Increases</a></li>
            <li><a href="#rent-calculator">Rent Control Calculator</a></li>
          </ul>
        </aside>

        <div class="prose-body">
          <h2 id="what">What rent control is</h2>
          <p>Ontario's <em>Residential Tenancies Act</em> caps how much a landlord can raise the rent on an existing tenant from one year to the next. The cap is called the <strong>annual rent increase guideline</strong>, and it's set by the provincial government every year.</p>

          <h2 id="covered">Which units are covered</h2>
          <p>Rent control applies to most residential units in Ontario that were <strong>first occupied as a residence before November 15, 2018</strong>.</p>
          <p>Units that were first occupied for residential use <strong>on or after November 15, 2018</strong> are <strong>exempt</strong>. The landlord of an exempt unit can raise the rent by any amount at the end of a fixed-term lease.</p>
          <div class="callout"><strong>Why this matters before you sign:</strong> a brand-new condo built in 2020 is not rent-controlled. A 1970s purpose-built apartment usually is. Over a multi-year stay, the difference can be thousands of dollars. I'll tell you which category a unit falls into before you commit.</div>

                    <details class="b60-section-toggle" id="guideline">
            <summary class="b60-section-toggle-summary">The annual guideline</summary>
            <div class="b60-section-body">
  <ul class="bullets">
              <li>The increase guideline is published every year by the Ontario Ministry of Municipal Affairs and Housing.</li>
              <li>Rent can only be increased <strong>once every 12 months</strong>.</li>
              <li>You must receive <strong>90 days' written notice</strong> of any increase, on the proper LTB form (<em>N1 — Notice of Rent Increase</em>).</li>
              <li>An increase that doesn't follow these rules is not legally enforceable.</li>
            </ul>
            </div>
          </details>

<details class="b60-section-toggle" id="agi">
            <summary class="b60-section-toggle-summary">Above-Guideline Increases (AGIs)</summary>
            <div class="b60-section-body">
  <p>A landlord can apply to the Landlord and Tenant Board (LTB) for a rent increase above the annual guideline. AGIs are usually granted for:</p>
            <ul class="bullets">
              <li>Extraordinary increases in municipal taxes or utilities</li>
              <li>Capital expenditures (major repairs or replacements to the building)</li>
              <li>New or expanded services to the building</li>
            </ul>
            <p>AGIs require LTB approval and tenants have the right to dispute the application.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <!-- ── Rent Control Calculator ────────────────────── -->
          <section class="rcc" id="rent-calculator" aria-labelledby="rcc-h">
            <h2 id="rcc-h">Rent Control Calculator</h2>
            <p class="rcc-lead">Enter your current rent and the current year's provincial guideline. The calculator shows the maximum new rent your landlord can charge for the coming year, and the maximum dollar increase. Ontario's <strong>2027 guideline is 1.9%</strong> — that's pre-filled so you can start with a real number.</p>

            <div class="rcc-grid">
              <div class="rcc-inputs">
                <div class="rcc-field">
                  <label for="rcc-rent">Current rent</label>
                  <div class="rcc-input-prefix">
                    <span>$</span>
                    <input id="rcc-rent" type="number" min="0" step="50" value="2200" inputmode="decimal" />
                    <span class="rcc-suffix">/ month</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="rcc-field">
                  <label for="rcc-pct">Provincial guideline %</label>
                  <div class="rcc-input-prefix">
                    <input id="rcc-pct" type="number" min="0" max="25" step="0.1" value="1.9" inputmode="decimal" />
                    <span class="rcc-suffix">%</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="rcc-outputs" aria-live="polite">
                <div class="rcc-out-card rcc-out-primary">
                  <div class="rcc-out-label">Maximum new rent</div>
                  <div class="rcc-out-value"><span id="rcc-new-rent">$2,241.80</span><span class="rcc-per"> / month</span></div>
                  <div class="rcc-out-sub">Your existing rent + the guideline%.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="rcc-out-card">
                  <div class="rcc-out-label">Maximum monthly increase</div>
                  <div class="rcc-out-value"><span id="rcc-delta">$41.80</span><span class="rcc-per"> / month</span></div>
                  <div class="rcc-out-sub">Anything above this needs an AGI approved by the LTB.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="rcc-out-card">
                  <div class="rcc-out-label">Annual increase</div>
                  <div class="rcc-out-value"><span id="rcc-annual">$501.60</span><span class="rcc-per"> / year</span></div>
                  <div class="rcc-out-sub">What the increase costs you over 12 months.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="rcc-fine">Reminder: the guideline only applies to units first occupied before <strong>November 15, 2018</strong>. If your unit is newer, there's no cap. Landlords must also give <strong>90 days' written notice</strong> on the correct form (N1) and can only raise once every 12 months.</p>
          </section>

<p class="legal-note">This guide is informational, not legal advice. For your specific situation, talk to a paralegal, a community legal clinic, or the LTB directly. I'm a registered real estate sales representative, not a lawyer.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection heading="Need a second set of eyes?" lead="If your landlord just raised your rent and you're not sure if it's legal, send me the notice. I'll tell you in 10 minutes whether it's valid or worth disputing." />
  <Footer />

<style>
  .rcc { margin: 32px 0 20px; padding: 24px 26px; background: #fafaf7; border: 1px solid var(--rule, #d8d4cc); border-radius: 14px; }
  .rcc h2 { font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 500; font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 8px; color: var(--ink, #1a1a1a); }
  .rcc-lead { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft, #4a4a4a); margin: 0 0 22px; }
  .rcc-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr; gap: 22px; align-items: start; }
  @media (max-width: 780px) { .rcc-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .rcc-inputs { display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .rcc-field label { display: block; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: var(--ink, #1a1a1a); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .rcc-input-prefix { display: flex; align-items: center; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--rule, #d8d4cc); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0 12px; transition: border-color 0.15s; }
  .rcc-input-prefix:focus-within { border-color: var(--accent, #b8845b); }
  .rcc-input-prefix > span { color: var(--ink-mute, #8a8a8a); font-size: 14px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .rcc-input-prefix input { border: 0; padding: 12px 8px; background: transparent; flex: 1; min-width: 0; font-size: 16px; font-family: inherit; color: var(--ink, #1a1a1a); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; outline: none; -moz-appearance: textfield; }
  .rcc-input-prefix input::-webkit-outer-spin-button, .rcc-input-prefix input::-webkit-inner-spin-button { -webkit-appearance: none; margin: 0; }
  .rcc-suffix { font-size: 12.5px; letter-spacing: 0.01em; }
  .rcc-outputs { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .rcc-out-card { padding: 14px 18px; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--rule, #d8d4cc); border-radius: 8px; }
  .rcc-out-primary { border-color: var(--accent, #b8845b); background: linear-gradient(180deg, #fdfaf3 0%, #fff 60%); }
  .rcc-out-label { font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-mute, #8a8a8a); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .rcc-out-value { font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--ink, #1a1a1a); line-height: 1.1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .rcc-out-primary .rcc-out-value { font-size: 34px; }
  .rcc-per { font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif; font-size: 0.5em; font-weight: 400; color: var(--ink-soft, #4a4a4a); margin-left: 4px; }
  .rcc-out-sub { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-soft, #4a4a4a); margin-top: 6px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .rcc-fine { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-mute, #8a8a8a); font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6; margin: 20px 0 0; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px dashed #d6d1c8; }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var rent = document.getElementById('rcc-rent');
    var pct  = document.getElementById('rcc-pct');
    if (!rent || !pct) return;
    var out = {
      newRent: document.getElementById('rcc-new-rent'),
      delta:   document.getElementById('rcc-delta'),
      annual:  document.getElementById('rcc-annual'),
    };
    function fmt(n) {
      return '$' + (Math.round(n * 100) / 100).toLocaleString('en-CA', { minimumFractionDigits: 2, maximumFractionDigits: 2 });
    }
    function compute() {
      var r = Math.max(0, parseFloat(rent.value) || 0);
      var p = Math.max(0, parseFloat(pct.value) || 0);
      var delta = r * (p / 100);
      out.newRent.textContent = fmt(r + delta);
      out.delta.textContent   = fmt(delta);
      out.annual.textContent  = fmt(delta * 12);
    }
    rent.addEventListener('input', compute);
    pct.addEventListener('input', compute);
    compute();
  })();
</script>
</BaseLayout>
